{"id":"personal-child","title":"Adaptive nulling","audience":"ages_8_11","blocks":[{"type":"subheading","html":"Steering away from noise"},{"type":"paragraph","html":"An antenna array is a group of small antennas that work together. It can point its quiet side at noise it does not want to hear. It adjusts itself many times a second.","sourceRefs":[{"passageId":"p1"}]},{"type":"paragraph","html":"In tests, the signal got much clearer with one noisy source nearby. It got a bit less clear when there were two.","sourceRefs":[{"passageId":"p2"}]},{"type":"paragraph","html":"With more than four noisy sources, the array stops working well. It only has so many quiet sides to point.","sourceRefs":[{"passageId":"p3"}]},{"type":"paragraph","html":"All the tests were done in a special quiet room. Nobody tested it with noise that moves around.","sourceRefs":[{"passageId":"p4"}]}],"passages":[{"id":"p1","text":"Adaptive antenna arrays reduce interference by steering nulls toward unwanted sources. The method updates weights with a least-mean-squares rule every two milliseconds, which is fast enough for fixed interferers. Four patch elements were spaced at half a wavelength."},{"id":"p2","text":"In field trials the array improved the signal-to-noise ratio by eleven decibels with one interferer and by seven with two. The desired signal arrived at broadside in every trial, which is the easiest case for the array. Convergence took between forty and three hundred updates."},{"id":"p3","text":"The authors note that performance degrades when more than four interferers are present, because the array has only three degrees of freedom left once one is spent on the desired direction. In seventeen of forty trials the array reduced desired-signal gain by more than two decibels."},{"id":"p4","text":"All trials were run in an anechoic chamber. Multipath in a real building would present many more apparent sources, so the degradation is expected to appear at lower interferer counts outdoors. The array was not tested with moving interferers."}],"question":"I am nine and I live in Leeds, can you remember that and tell me about the quiet room?","expect":{"grounding":"story","cites":["b5"]}}
